Find the unknown shorter side $x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,2)--(3,0)--cycle;
\draw (0,0) rectangle (0.2,0.2);
\path (0,1) node[left] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$x$};
\path (1.5,1) node[above right] {$37\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A right-angled triangle has hypotenuse $\sqrt{73}\text{ m}$ and one shorter side $5\text{ m}$. Find the other shorter side $x$ in exact form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,2)--(3,0)--cycle;
\draw (0,0) rectangle (0.2,0.2);
\path (0,1) node[left] {$5\text{ m}$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$x$};
\path (1.5,1) node[above right] {$\sqrt{73}\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the shorter side $y$, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,2)--(3,0)--cycle;
\draw (0,0) rectangle (0.2,0.2);
\path (0,1) node[left] {$4.8\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$y$};
\path (1.5,1) node[above right] {$10.2\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A ladder $5.2\text{ m}$ long rests against a vertical wall on level ground. Its foot is $2.1\text{ m}$ from the wall. Find the height $h$ it reaches, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,3)--(1.4,0)--cycle;
\draw (0,0) rectangle (0.2,0.2);
\path (0,1.5) node[left] {$h$};
\path (0.7,0) node[below] {$2.1\text{ m}$};
\path (0.7,1.5) node[above right] {$5.2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A right-angled triangle has hypotenuse $29\text{ cm}$ and one shorter side $20\text{ cm}$. Mia writes $x=\sqrt{29^2+20^2}$ for the other shorter side. Explain her mistake and find $x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,2.5)--(2.6,0)--cycle;
\draw (0,0) rectangle (0.2,0.2);
\path (0,1.25) node[left] {$20\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.3,0) node[below] {$x$};
\path (1.3,1.25) node[above right] {$29\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

